    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.2/p@103786",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LEAR.\nBlow, winds, and crack your cheeks! Rage! blow!\nYou cataracts and hurricanoes, spout\nTill you have drench’d our steeples, drown’d the cocks!\nYou sulphurous and thought-executing fires,\nVaunt-couriers to oak-cleaving thunderbolts,\nSinge my white head! And thou, all-shaking thunder,\nStrike flat the thick rotundity o’ the world!\nCrack nature’s moulds, all germens spill at once,\nThat make ingrateful man!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
