    {
      "id": "king-lear/sceneIII_18.2/p@106905",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "KENT.\nAlack, bareheaded!\nGracious my lord, hard by here is a hovel;\nSome friendship will it lend you ’gainst the tempest:\nRepose you there, whilst I to this hard house,—\nMore harder than the stones whereof ’tis rais’d;\nWhich even but now, demanding after you,\nDenied me to come in,—return, and force\nTheir scanted courtesy.",
